<h1>The license, plainly</h1>

<p class="lede">pālana is licensed under the
<a href="https://github.com/sageframe-no-kaji/palana/blob/main/LICENSE">GPL-3.0</a>.
This page says what that means in practice, in the order the questions come
up.</p>

<section>
<h2 id="you-can">What you can do without asking<a class="hlink" href="#you-can">#</a></h2>

<p>Use pālana for anything. Read every line of the source. Build it yourself —
<code>swift build</code> and go. Modify it. Fork it. Redistribute it, including
any signed build, as long as the source travels with it under the same
license. None of this requires permission; that is what the license is.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2 id="no-cla">No CLA, ever<a class="hlink" href="#no-cla">#</a></h2>

<p>Contributions are accepted under GPL-3.0 and contributors keep their
copyright. There is no contributor license agreement and there never will be
one. The consequence is deliberate: once outside contributions are in the
code, nobody—including the author—can relicense pālana closed. Your patches
lock it open.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2 id="the-name">The code is free. The name identifies the author's builds.<a class="hlink" href="#the-name">#</a></h2>

<p>Forks are welcome and must travel under their own name. "pālana" and the
leaf mark identify builds signed, notarized, and released by the author—that
signature chain is the one thing a fork cannot carry, and the name is how you
know which builds carry it.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2 id="paid">The price at 1.0<a class="hlink" href="#paid">#</a></h2>

<p>The beta is free. At 1.0, signed builds become a one-time $29 purchase—no
subscription, no license key, all 1.x updates included—and the license does
not change: the code stays GPL-3.0, building it yourself stays free, and the
purchase pays for the signing certificate, the notarization, and the time.
The GPL explicitly permits selling copies—what it forbids is closing the
source, and that door is <a href="#no-cla">welded shut above</a>.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2 id="redistributing">If you redistribute<a class="hlink" href="#redistributing">#</a></h2>

<p>Keep the license, keep the notices, and provide the source—a link to
<a href="https://github.com/sageframe-no-kaji/palana">the repo</a> at the
matching version satisfies it. The
<a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html">full text</a> governs
where this page simplifies.</p>
</section>
